+---
+id: dl-001-deterministic-per-list-counter-for-task-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Deterministic per-list counter for task ids"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks needed a stable identifier that survives a rename (`rename` currently re-keys the list's
+internal map by title, so the old title stops resolving). `src/domain/` must not read the clock or
+generate random identifiers (`r3-no-clock-or-randomness`), which rules out the obvious choices:
+`Date.now()`-based ids, `Math.random()`, `crypto.randomUUID()`.
+
+Also needed: a way to resolve either a title or an id on the methods that currently take a title
+(`find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`, `remove`), plus a new `get(id)` for id-only
+lookup.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Generate ids with a plain incrementing counter private to each `createTaskList()` closure, formatted
+  as `` `t${n}` ``. It is deterministic, has no dependency on wall-clock or randomness, and is unique
+  for the lifetime of that list instance (the counter never resets or reuses a value, even after a
+  `remove`).
+- The counter only advances on a successful `add` (after the duplicate-title check), so a rejected
+  `add` does not burn an id.
+- `find`-and-friends resolve their `identifier` argument by trying it as a title first (exact match on
+  the map key, which is how the list already stores tasks), then falling back to an id lookup. This
+  keeps every existing title-based call working unchanged, and only matters for the edge case of a
+  title that happens to collide with another task's id string, which titles win.
+- `get(id)` is a separate, narrower method: id-only, no title fallback, since its contract is "look up
+  by the id I was handed," not "accept whatever string the user typed."
+- `rename` was restructured to look the task up once up front (by title or id) and compare the
+  requested new title against the *found task's* current title, rather than assuming its first
+  argument literally is that title — it might now be an id instead.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `createTask` takes `id` as an explicit second parameter; callers (only `list.ts`) own id generation,
+  keeping `task.ts` free of any notion of a counter or list-wide uniqueness.
+- `Task.id` is preserved automatically through every transform (`completeTask`, `reopenTask`,
+  `renameTask`, `addTag`, `removeTag`) because they all return `{ ...task, ... }` shallow copies.
+- No new dependency was needed (satisfies `r1-no-new-dependency`); no `Date`/`Math.random` calls were
+  introduced (satisfies `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`).
