+---
+id: task-001-add-stable-task-ids
+type: task
+title: "Add stable task ids"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Give each task a unique identifier that keeps working after the task is renamed.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `Task` (`src/domain/task.ts`) gained a required `id: string` field. `createTask(input, id)` now
+  takes the id as an explicit parameter instead of generating one itself.
+- `createTaskList()` (`src/domain/list.ts`) assigns each added task an id from an in-memory counter
+  (`t1`, `t2`, …), scoped to that list instance, never reused. This keeps id generation deterministic,
+  with no clock or randomness, as required for code under `src/domain/`.
+- `TaskList` gained a `get(id)` method: a `Result<Task>` lookup by id only, `not-found` otherwise.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` now accept either a task's title
+  or its id (their parameter is renamed `identifier`). Title match is tried first, then id, so existing
+  callers that pass a title keep working unchanged.
+- `rename` was rewritten to look the task up once (by title or id) before comparing the new title
+  against the current one, instead of assuming its first argument is literally the stored title.
+- Tasks keep their id across every mutation, since `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag`
+  and `removeTag` all return a shallow copy of the existing task (`{ ...task, ... }`), carrying the id
+  along automatically.
+
+## Tests
+
+Added to `test/list.test.ts`: unique ids on add, `get` happy path and not-found, finding a renamed task
+by its old id, completing/reopening/tagging/untagging by id, and removing by id. Updated the existing
+"adds an open task" test to expect the new `id` field. `npm test` passes (11 `it` blocks, all green).
